---
description: Change-aware CI; a PR merges and a Release ships only when the four required checks are green
globs: .github/workflows/**,tools/ci_scope.py,tools/test_ci_scope*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# CI selection contract

- Classify the complete PR merge-base diff, including deleted paths and both sides
  of renames. Pushes compare before/after; manual runs verify everything.
- Documentation and site-only changes run docs/agent validation and secret scanning.
  Documentation is Markdown at the root or under `docs/` / `knowledge/`, plus images
  under `docs/` (`.png .webp .jpg .jpeg .gif .svg`: README screenshots and diagrams).
  Nothing packages `docs/`, so a README image never builds or publishes a release.
- Frontend changes run lint, unit tests, build, Chromium E2E and desktop packaging.
  Trading-facing frontend modules also run the full backend suite.
- Backend changes run the full backend suite (including execution, risk, short,
  idempotency and live opt-in gates), Chromium E2E and desktop packaging.
- Electron, build scripts, dependency manifests, CI, tools and unknown paths run
  all application checks. Never infer a safe skip from a missing/failed diff.
- Merging is green only (owner decision 2026-10-13, "Merge only green PRs too").
  `Auto-merge` `needs` Backend tests, Frontend build, Frontend E2E and Agent contract
  and `decide()` (`tools/pr_checks.py`) merges only when each concluded success at
  its newest run on the head; a red one holds with a PR comment, a running one waits.
  Scope never skips one of the four at GitHub's level: an inapplicable job concludes
  success after "Unaffected", so docs-only PRs merge. Branch protection has no
  required status checks (the merge job is the gate). Keep force-push/deletion blocked.
- Releasing is green only too (owner decision 2026-10-13). Desktop pack's
  `verify` job (`Release checks`) calls `deploy.yml` with `full: true` on the commit
  it packed, so nothing is scope-skipped; `Publish vNNN installer` runs
  `tools/release_gate.py` first and publishes only when the pack and Backend tests,
  Frontend build, Frontend E2E and Agent contract concluded success at their latest
  attempt. Anything else -- skipped included -- fails it with "vNNN not published:
  <check> ...". The security scanners stay warning-only and never hold a Release.
- Check names remain stable for visibility. Jobs report classification failures;
  inapplicable heavy steps are skipped with a reason. Red stays visible, not disguised.
- Windows packaging runs only for application-affecting changes, a release tag, or
  manual dispatch. PRs affecting packaging attempt the installer without delaying
  merge. Every master commit is tagged `vNNN`; a green application-affecting one
  also publishes its GitHub Release (operator decision 2026-09-23, supersedes #347's
  tag-only publishing). Docs/site-only pushes pack nothing and get the tag only; a
  PR merged by Actions is dispatched, which selects everything, so it packs and is
  released once green even when it only changed docs.
- Keep secret scanning on every PR. Advisory source scanners run on source changes;
  dependency scanning runs on manifest changes; all run daily and on manual dispatch.
- Repository branch cleanup/protection audits belong in scheduled maintenance,
  never the PR Agent contract gate. Tests of those tools remain in that gate.
- Cancel superseded PR CI; do not cancel master runs (CI groups non-PR runs by commit,
  so a release's call never waits on or cancels another's). Bound every job with a timeout.
- No production trading configuration or test assertion may be weakened to speed CI.
- Security discovery follows the explicitly called local security workflow so moving
  scanners does not create false missing-scanner findings.
- Drafts, do-not-merge, forks and actual merge conflicts retain their existing holds.
  Auto-merge runs master's merge tool, never the PR's own copy of the gate.
